<%- include('../partials/header') %>
<main id="main"><div class="shell"><section class="section">
  <h1 class="section__title">Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <h3>Is this the real National Prisons Information Portal?</h3>
    <p>No. It is an unofficial local demonstration replica. It cannot book a visit, file a
    grievance, or reach any prison.</p>
    <h3>Is the data real?</h3>
    <p>No. Every record is synthetic, generated by <code>replica/database/seed.js</code>.
    The option lists (states, relationships, identity proof types) are transcribed from the
    original&rsquo;s public form markup, so the value domain matches.</p>
    <h3>Why do some pages look simpler than the original?</h3>
    <p>Where the original&rsquo;s behaviour sits behind a login, a CAPTCHA or its server code, it
    could not be observed and is not guessed at. <code>analysis/replication_gaps.json</code>
    lists every such gap.</p>
    <h3>Where did the field rules come from?</h3>
    <p>From the rendered markup of the live forms. Rules marked <code>[REC]</code> in
    <code>replica/backend/validation.js</code> are this replica&rsquo;s own choices, not the
    original&rsquo;s requirements.</p>
  </div>
</section></div></main>
<%- include('../partials/footer') %>
